# IMPLEMENTATION_STEPS: cu-008

1. Change `pipelines/enrichment/build.sbt` to add hadoop-aws at the version Spark 3.5.1 was built against, scoped Provided, using CrossVersion.for3Use2_13 because the artifact ships Scala 2.13 only.

```scala
      ("org.apache.hadoop" % "hadoop-aws" % "3.3.4" % Provided).cross(CrossVersion.for3Use2_13),
```

   Prove: `grep -q 'hadoop-aws' pipelines/enrichment/build.sbt && cd pipelines/enrichment && sbt compile`

2. Change `pipelines/enrichment/src/main/scala/newspipe/control/dependencyInjection/AppContainer.scala` so the SparkSession builder receives the four fs.s3a settings, read from EnvConfig rather than hardcoded.

```scala
package newspipe.control.dependencyInjection

import newspipe.application.services.EnrichmentService
import newspipe.infrastructure.bronze.DeltaMergeSink
import newspipe.infrastructure.env.EnvConfig
import newspipe.infrastructure.kafka.KafkaRawConsumer
import newspipe.infrastructure.llmdataenricher.OpenCodeCliClient
import org.apache.spark.sql.SparkSession

import java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit
import scala.concurrent.duration.FiniteDuration

final class AppContainer(env: EnvConfig):
  val spark: SparkSession = SparkSession.builder()
    .appName("newspipe-enrichment")
    .master(env.sparkMaster)
    .config("spark.sql.extensions", "io.delta.sql.DeltaSparkSessionExtension")
    .config("spark.sql.catalog.spark_catalog", "org.apache.spark.sql.delta.catalog.DeltaCatalog")
    .config("spark.hadoop.fs.s3a.endpoint", env.s3Endpoint)
    .config("spark.hadoop.fs.s3a.path.style.access", env.s3PathStyle.toString)
    .config("spark.hadoop.fs.s3a.access.key", env.s3AccessKey)
    .config("spark.hadoop.fs.s3a.secret.key", env.s3SecretKey)
    .getOrCreate()
  val consumer = new KafkaRawConsumer(env.kafkaBootstrap, env.rawTopic, env.groupId)
  val enrich = new OpenCodeCliClient(env.opencodeModel, FiniteDuration(env.opencodeTimeoutSeconds, TimeUnit.SECONDS))
  val sink = new DeltaMergeSink(spark, env.bronzePath)
  val service = new EnrichmentService(consumer, enrich, sink)

  def close(): Unit =
    consumer.close()
    spark.stop()
```

   Prove: `grep -c 'fs.s3a' pipelines/enrichment/src/main/scala/newspipe/control/dependencyInjection/AppContainer.scala && cd pipelines/enrichment && sbt compile`

3. Run the enrichment suite so MergeBackfillSpec, which builds its own session, is proven undisturbed.

```sh
cd pipelines/enrichment && sbt test
```

   Prove: `cd pipelines/enrichment && sbt test | tail -5`

